<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .iran-media-badge { font-size: 0.75em; background: rgba(142, 68, 173, 0.15); border: 1px solid var(--iran); color: var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 8px; }
  .inside-iran p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .inside-iran p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 20px; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 14px; padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; margin-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; min-width: 220px; }
  .regime-row .p { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 1.1em; color: var(--accent3); min-width: 80px; }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.88em; color: var(--text-muted); flex: 1; min-width: 200px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .sources-list li { font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .source-tier { font-size: 0.72em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); color: var(--red); border: 1px solid var(--red); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { margin-top: 20px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 8px 0; }
  .expert-body { padding: 14px 0; }
  .expert-quote { background: var(--card); border-left: 3px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 0.88em; color: var(--text); }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  footer { text-align: center; padding: 30px 20px; font-size: 0.78em; color: var(--text-muted); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 20px; }
  .next-update { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">31 August 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 185</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-08-31T07:30:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL (written LAST by Judge) ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Active military escalation: <span class="cite">F5</span> resolved NO after CENTCOM struck Larak Island on Iranian sovereign territory (Aug 30) and Iran's IRGC launched approximately 32 ballistic missiles at US bases in Jordan (Aug 31) — the ceasefire lasted 29 days. <span class="cite">F8</span> now tracks whether a strike pause can re-establish before Sep 14 (p=0.38), while <span class="cite">F2</span> is at 0.08 and <span class="cite">F1</span> at 0.27, the diplomatic track near-collapsed.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">6 active · 2 resolved today · last reasoned 2026-08-31</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-term (≤72h)</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F1 · 2026-08-30-iran-mfa-hormuz-conditions-by-sep-02</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran's Foreign Ministry issue a formal public statement of specific conditions for reopening the Strait of Hormuz before EOD 2026-09-02?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">27%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">↓ −18pp from 45% (2026-08-30)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-02</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Iran's MFA bandwidth is consumed by the Larak Island strike response; Baghaei statements in the Aug 30 window are general declarations, not a formal enumerated-conditions MFA press-conference statement; both indicators remain NOT_OBSERVED; Mojtaba Khamenei's Aug 30 letter runs contrary to a conditions-publication posture; 48h horizon with no observable trajectory toward a formal IRNA-attributed enumeration.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Iran's Foreign Ministry spokesperson or Araghchi issues a formal public statement via IRNA, MFA press conference, or state-broadcast listing specific named conditions for reopening Hormuz, before EOD 2026-09-02.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IRNA or official MFA transcript plus one TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP) carrying the statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>SNSC/IRGC spokespeople without MFA imprimatur = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Unnamed-source lists = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Restatements of existing general positions = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran MFA formal IRNA-attributed statement with enumerated conditions</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran-Oman MOU text attributed to MFA formal channel</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F2 · 2026-08-30-us-iran-hormuz-deal-by-sep-14</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a publicly acknowledged formal US-Iran Hormuz reopening agreement be signed or formally acknowledged by named officials on both sides before EOD 2026-09-14?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">8%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">↓ −17pp from 25% (2026-08-30)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-14</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Active military exchange as of Aug 30-31 — CENTCOM Larak strike on Iranian sovereign territory, IRGC ballistic missile response on US Jordan bases — renders a formal signed Hormuz agreement before Sep 14 near-impossible. Mojtaba Khamenei's Aug 30 "real enemy" letter is directly contrary to the approval posture Axios (Aug 5) identified as the blocking condition for deal formalization. Larak re-mining evidence erodes confidence in the implementation track.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a TIER1 source reports a signed or publicly acknowledged formal agreement between named US and Iranian officials (Witkoff-Araghchi or Vance-level) committing both parties to specific Hormuz reopening terms, before EOD 2026-09-14.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP/Axios/Bloomberg plus State Dept or Iranian MFA official statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Oral agreements in-principle = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Framework documents under negotiation = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Ceasefire extensions without Hormuz-specific terms = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">TIER1 report of a convened Witkoff-Araghchi or equivalent signing session</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Mojtaba Khamenei public statement endorsing the Araghchi-Oman Hormuz framework</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F8 · 2026-08-31-us-iran-strike-pause-by-sep-14</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a continuous pause in direct US-Iran strikes hold from 2026-08-31 through EOD 2026-09-14?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">NEW — opening</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-14</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast replacing F5 (RESOLVED-NO). CENTCOM's Larak Island strike (Aug 30) and IRGC's ~32-missile response on US Jordan bases (Aug 31) ended the Aug 2 ceasefire. Both sides have now struck sovereign or near-sovereign installations, raising costs of continued exchange. Mediator channels (Qatar PM, Oman working group) remain nominally active. Iranian economic conditions and Mojtaba Khamenei's injury-induced operational constraints favor a pause. Against: IRGC retaliation posture post-Larak and domestic political constraints from Mojtaba's Aug 30 "real enemy" letter. Opening probability 0.38.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if no TIER1-confirmed direct US strike on Iranian sovereign territory AND no Iranian strike on US military facilities or Israeli territory occurs in any 24h window from 2026-08-31 through EOD 2026-09-14. Both conditions must hold continuously; a single confirmed incident resolves NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two independent TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNN/Al Jazeera) OR one TIER1 plus official US (CENTCOM) or Iranian (IRGC/MFA) statement.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Proxy strikes by Hezbollah/Houthi without confirmed direct US-Iran exchange = no resolution. Disputed strike lacking two independent TIER1 confirmations = AMBIGUOUS, hold 48h. Strikes on named US military installations count; ambiguous non-sovereign territory requires CENTCOM or TIER1 confirmation.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">72h window passes without TIER1-confirmed direct US-Iran exchange</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar or Oman mediator public statement of active strike-pause negotiation</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3 · 2026-08-30-iran-iaea-full-access-by-sep-30</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the IAEA Director General confirm physical inspector access to all major Iranian nuclear sites before EOD 2026-09-30?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">↓ −13pp from 35% (2026-08-30)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Nuclear track frozen by active military exchange (Larak/Jordan Aug 30-31). Baghaei (June 19) ruled out IAEA access to war-damaged sites with no schedule. IAEA DG Grossi's "inspections will happen after a deal" framing (June 24) is unchanged. Structural repair: Annex B site list replaced by explicit enumeration (Natanz FEP/PFEP, Fordow, Isfahan IFEP, Arak, Parchin) to resolve Judge Flag on criteria computability.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IAEA DG confirms physical inspector access to all of: Natanz FEP, Natanz PFEP, Fordow, Isfahan IFEP, Arak IR-40, and Parchin — before EOD 2026-09-30. All named sites required; partial access does not qualify.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Official IAEA statement (iaea.org) plus one TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/Al Jazeera).</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Partial access to subset of named sites = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Agreed-in-principle without physical entry = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. If IAEA DG characterizes access as "complete" at resolution date, resolve per DG's characterization.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IAEA DG formal statement confirming physical entry to at least one named site</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran MFA lifts its June 19 ruling against IAEA access to war-damaged sites</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4 · 2026-08-30-hormuz-24-transits-by-oct-15</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Hormuz reach a 7-day average of ≥24 commercial transits/day before EOD 2026-10-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">↓ −18pp from 40% (2026-08-30)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Larak Island strike (Aug 30, CENTCOM) proved IRGC can deploy assets to threaten cleared lanes within the corridor CENTCOM declared mine-free Aug 27. Commercial operators and P&I underwriters face materially higher uncertainty about lane permanence. USNI News (Aug 28) records 16.3/day 7-day average — directional progress but 47% below the 24/day YES threshold. P&I war-risk cover reinstatement remains NOT_OBSERVED and is the principal gateway for mainstream commercial traffic.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Lloyd's List Intelligence or IMF PortWatch records a 7-day rolling average of ≥24 commercial transits/day through Hormuz in any consecutive 7-day window between 2026-08-30 and 2026-10-15.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Lloyd's List Intelligence plus one corroborating Bloomberg/Reuters/USNI source.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Naval-escorted convoys count if cargo is commercial. Single days above 24 without a 7-day average do not qualify. If Lloyd's List unpublished, use best AIS tracker and flag AMBIGUOUS if sources conflict by more than 20%.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-OBSERVED">Lloyd's List 7-day avg above 15 transits/day — CONFIRMED at 16.3/day (USNI Aug 28)</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">P&I war-risk cover reinstated by major Lloyd's underwriters for Hormuz transit</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM mine-free declaration translated to Lloyd's removal from war-risk zones</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 6-12 MONTHS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 Months</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
